  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The orbitals which have same energy are called&nbsp;degenerate orbitals. Energy or an orbital depends on two quantum numbers, principle quantum number (n) and azimuthal quantum number (l).</p><p>The orbitals with similar values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math> but with different value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;will be degenerate orbitals.</p><p>Among the given set or orbital only option (B)&nbsp;fulfil this condition.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
  }
